  "title": "India's Expansion of Small Modular Reactors and Defence Modernization",
  "summary": "India plans to expand its nuclear energy capacity, including the development of at least five indigenous small modular reactors by 2033, aiming to replace fossil fuel plants and infrastructure. The Nuclear Energy Mission targets 100 GWe of nuclear capacity by 2047. Rajnath Singh highlighted India's progress in modernizing its military infrastructure and boosting defence exports, with key initiatives such as 'Aatmanirbhar Bharat' and 'Make in India' driving economic growth and military capability.",
